error[E-ambiguous-tolerance]: ambiguous tolerance
  --> follow_on.spl:5:13
  |
5 |     let i = capacity / 2h ± 10%;
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ does `±` apply to this whole expression?
  |
  = help: `(capacity / 2h) ± 10%` for a spread on the result
  = help: `capacity / (2h ± 10%)` for a spread on one term

error[E-unit-suffix]: unknown unit `h`
  --> follow_on.spl:5:25
  |
5 |     let i = capacity / 2h ± 10%;
  |                         ^ not a unit or prefix
  |
  = help: did you mean `H`?
  = note: units are V A Ω F H Hz s W K °C % dB, optionally after a prefix f p n u µ m k M G T (case matters)

